\f3\fs26 The vid phone screamed, demanding Cracker\'92s attention. The Elvi had urgent news for the Great Teacher, but were unable to get access to the management zone to speak to him in person. \
\'93Hello? This is\'85actually I don\'92t know who I am supposed to be, who is calling?\'94 Cracker said without confidence or authority.\
\'93It\'92s Elvis, Great Teacher.\'94\
\'93Ahh, you are going to have to be a bit more specific.\'94 \
\'93Elvis-in-charge of the tunneling team, sir, we have hit a bit of a snag. We have cracked a sewer main and it is leaking badly, threatening to burst at any moment.\'94\
 \'93How far from the completion are you?\'94\
\'93We have already hit the underside of the basement. We only have to crack the floor, about 1 metre of steel reinforced concrete. It should not take that long, but we are concerned about flooding. The tunnel is slowly filling and the stench is unbearable, but the smell is not the biggest problem. We are not only concerned with the possibility of suffocation, but when we crack the floor we will be endangered by the bio-agents stored there in the lab. We have been screaming out for the bio-suits for the last week, but it has fallen upon deaf ears, Great Teacher. We need you to get the suits here fast.\'94\
 \
\'93Have no concern other than the task at hand. Dig in short shifts, say 1 hour for each team. Shorten the length of time if necessary, but do not crack the floor. I will chase up the suits and deliver them myself. Consider it done, my Elvi brother.\'94 Cracker was feeling very guilty. He had taken on the supervisory role with the promise that no Elvi would be harmed, but had been so pre-occupied with the capture of Haloren Smythe and he had not visited the work-site for nearly ten days. He had ordered the suits weeks ago and had been assured that the treasury would release the funds forthwith. He was weighed down by the shame of failing his brothers and was determined to promptly resolve the issue, giving the treasurer a kick the the backside for good measure. \
\'93Thank you, Great Teacher.\'94\
Cracker ended the conversation and contacted Sarah with some urgency. \'93Hey, Mrs Shakti, what\'92s up\'94\
\'93Cracker, good to see you. How can I help the Great Teacher today?\'94 Sarah was jovial, precisely as Cracker expected.\
\'93Is your line secure at your end?\'94\
\'93Yes, I am yet to move out of my apartment.\'94\
\'93The Elvi are just about to break into the lab, but have no protective gear. There are no bio-suits, emergency showers, radiation gel or even the incendiary grenades. We need to see the High Elvis and his ministers. I was told everything was under control, but someone has dropped the ball and placed my digging team in danger.\'94\
\'93They have made terrific progress, but it will be for naught unless we can access the lab safely. I will contact the High Elvis and get him to shake some coin out of the treasurer. I get the impression the treasurer thinks the money is his and is trying to save the Elvi nation on a shoestring. I will call you back shortly. Great Teacher? Good to hear from you.\'94 Sarah had also been pre-occupied since her allocation ceremony. \
Cracker only had to wait a few minutes for the return call from Sarah. \'93Yes, Cracker we have a major problem. The suits were never ordered and the explosives cannot be obtained until next week. The Minister for the Treasury says you never ordered the suits and he knows nothing about it. There will be no suits, no safety showers and worst of all, no explosives.\'94\
\'93That\'92s complete crap. I spoke to him personally, weeks ago.\'94 Cracker was aghast.\
\'93I guessed as much. He\'92s a politician now and will point the finger in any direction except his own. I will meet you at the work site straight away. Bring your tunneling gear, Great Teacher.\'94\
\'93See you soon, Blessed Mother.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi720\sl360\slmult1\qc\partightenfactor0

