\f3\fs26 Cracker had only been on site a few minutes when Sarah arrived, her protruding belly was round and taught. Far too distracted by the impasse the present circumstances had created, she did not notice the approach of Cracker until he was upon her.\
\'93Oh,Cracker, you got here fast.\'94 She knew the time had come to tell him of the T-virus and had been practicing what she would say all the way to the site, but now all those well rehearsed words had sublimated into the ether. \'93I have something to confess.\'94\
\'93This doesn\'92t sound promising.\'94 He knew coming clean, at least from the very few times he had given it a lash, was a dirty business and rarely went well for either party.\
\'93Please don\'92t interrupt. This is going to be difficult enough as it is. Do you remember your remarkable transformation the night you removed the disc from under my skin?\'94\
\'93It\'92s on my highlights reel.\'94\
\'93I did not need to know that, thank you. I told you I thought the disc had done something to you, but that was a lie.\'94 She baulked for a second or two, second guessing the decision to purge her conscience. \'93Oh dear, it is all so tawdry. When I was about 12 years old my mother was in a relationship with a very nice, virologist. They were in love, at least that what it seemed like to me. He was always sending her flowers and presents, but he never thought to send me or my sister anything, not even an e-card when my twelfth birthday came along. A few weeks later, I was at home when a package arrived for my mother. Another gift! I knew it was wrong, but I so wanted a present for myself. Mother was not home, so I opened it up and found a short note and a vial containing a clear liquid. The note read drink the vial, which I did without hesitation, not being bothered to read the rest of the message. My immature taste buds salivated with anticipation of a sugary treat, but it was near tasteless and I dismissed it as water. Reading on I was sickened to discover the vial contained the three doses of the T-virus, a contagion transmitted by blood or other bodily fluids such as semen. I knew the vial did not contain blood, so naturally I thought I had swallowed a vial of semen and really freaked out. I remember with absolute clarity the disgust I felt. He had given me a STD! I was a 12 year old virgin with a social disease!\'94\
\'93Ah, hence the virginity thing.\'94 
\f5\i The Dawkins would weep! 
\f3\i0 \
\'93The virginity thing? Can you imagine how I felt?\'94 \
\'93Well, if this conversation is going in the direction I think it is, I know exactly how you felt. What did you tell your mother?\'94\
\'93I never said a word. I was too frightened to tell her. Her boyfriend never called again and she never spoke of him again.\'94\
\'93So I got the virus from you when I removed the disc?\'94\
\'93There is no doubt.\'94\
\'93Well worth it.\'94 He smiled. 
\f5\i Well worth it. 
\f3\i0 \
\'93I am so sorry.\'94\
\'93Are you kidding? Since then I have never felt better. I\'92ve got a six pack now and I don\'92t do any exercise. I mean, none at all. I got shot three times and survived! Sarah, you did me one big favour. Am I correct in assuming the virus is behind all of this?\'94\
\'93Yes. Everything in my body operates at a significantly more efficient rate than the average person.\'94\
\'93Understatement. But why are you telling me this now? We have to work out how we are going to get those Elvi into that lab safely.\'94 Cracker wanted his Elvi safe and sound.\
\'93We don\'92t. None of the Elvi are going in. It is just too dangerous. You and I have to go in, no suits, no protection.\'94\
\'93I can\'92t let you go in there, it\'92s suicide.\'94\
\'93I don\'92t think so. I think we are the only two that can enter the lab safely. I am willing to bet the T-virus will give us sufficient protection.\'94\
\'93You are willing to bet our lives and the life of the little Dawkins?\'94\
\'93Either that or you get to pick which Elvi get to go in our place. Is that a decision you want to make?\'94\
\'93No, I can\'92t face that.\'94 Picking who gets to die, while he gets to live, was far too cowardly for Cracker to consider. \'93If we get infected by anything nasty, we could be in there for quite a while before we get the all clear. If we were ever let out.\'94\
\'93Yes, I have considered that, but who is going to stop us?\'94 \
\'93No one, I guess.\'94 He did not like the idea of being stuck indefinitely in a bio-weapons bunker any better than Sarah. \'93Site supervisor, I need to speak with the site supervisor.\'94 Cracker asked generally of the Elvi present.\
\'93Of course Great Teacher, he is in the tunnel\'94\
\'93The Blessed Mother and I need to speak with him now.\'94 Cracker commanded and the one of the labourers headed off into the tunnel returning a few minutes later with the digging crew. The Site Manager Elvis in a dull blue safety vest approached and stood reverently, safety helmet politely removed and held to his stomach in both hands  He reeked terribly of sweat and sewage and was completely soaked by both.\
\'93Blessed Mother and the Great Teacher. You honour me.\'94 He bowed humbly to his venerated leaders.\
\'93Elvis, we do not have the safety equipment I promised. The funds were never released and the gear was never delivered. I am so very sorry.\'94 Cracker, the Great Teacher, was genuinely and profoundly contrite. \
\'93We will carry on regardless. All my Elvi are prepared for whatever is in there. We are all prepared to die to protect our people.\'94 The site manager was deadly serious. Each man and women in the digging team had contemplated the horrors awaiting inside the laboratory and volunteered anyway, knowing that every other Elvi would do the same without question.\
\'93No, it was my responsibility. I made the arrangements, but failed to follow up and this is the result. I cannot and will not allow anyone to place themselves in danger because I of my neglect.\'94 Cracker was mortified that he had let this situation arise. \'93The Blessed Mother has a plan that will place none of you in danger.\'94 \
\'93The Great Teacher and I, alone, will be present when the basement floor of the lab is cracked. We will take the risk and we will bear the brunt of anything that befalls us.\'94 Sarah explained, cloaked in an invisible aura radiating confidence and authority that was difficult to resist.\
\'93Blessed mother, no. You are pregnant. You cannot place yourself or the one-after-the-one in danger. That is precisely why we are here. We are the cannon fodder in this cold war and eminently expendable. You are far more important than any one individual Elvis.\'94\
\'93This is not a request, Elvis. You are instructed to removed all your men and women from the tunnel and seal the entrance.\'94 The Great Teacher decided the debate was over.\
\'93There is no need to seal the tunnel. As you ordered, Great Teacher, it was dug at a slight upward grade for about 50 metres before we had to dig down and under a mass of cables, pipes and conduits. Essentially we have created a giant \'93U \'94 bend that is now filled with sewer and waste water. Contaminated air is blocked by the water and cannot get out. To get in there you will have to swim through about 20 metres of raw sewage. The air on the other side is toxic, we are pumping in fresh air through a hose, but it has had limited effect. You will be forced to retreat before succumbing to the fumes.\'94\
\'93We will have to take our chances. Is all the digging equipment ready to go?\'94 Cracker tried to be all business, but in reality he was just plain terrified. \
\'93Every hand tool, jack hammer, grinder and drill we have is sitting there idle at the moment. At least allow me to accompany you, Blessed mother. I fear I will be branded a coward if I do otherwise.\'94\
\'93I cannot allow that, Elvis.\'94 The Blessed Mother hugged him gently and caring not for the fetor rising from his bedraggled frame, she placed her hands on each of his cheeks, \'93No one could ever accuse the Elvi of cowardice. You humble me with your fealty, something I do not deserve.\'94 Elvis began to weep. Hands had been placed upon him by the Blessed mother and had felt her grace.\
They made their way toward the entrance of the tunnel, the Elvi present exchanged perplexed looks of shock and amazement as the two great leaders of their movement navigated toward dangers untold. Having just made the return journey themselves, they were acutely aware of the repugnant, nauseating swim their leaders were about to embark upon, faces silently pleading for their pregnant leader not to enter. None of them wanted to be a bystander at the death of the Blessed Mother and they desperately wanted to be somewhere far, far away. \
The easy stroll up the slight grade, belied the horror that awaited just over the rise where the floor angled sharply downward to a pool of bacteria and filth. Cracker\'92s eye\'92s felt the sting of the vapours and was already gagging when he entered the sludge. He tried to draw in a deep breath, but coughed and spluttered as tussive miasma attacked his delicate lung tissue. He managed, with some difficultly, to hold down a second deep breath and waded in, trying desperately to think of something else, anything else and hoping he would not suffer a coughing fit while fully submerged. Eyes and mouth firmly shut he swam like a blackened slime toad, through the molasses thick filth, bumping into walls and the bottoming out on the floor before finding his way, in the darkness, to the surface on the far side. The air was thick with putrid particles, methane vapours and stink of every kind. He thought the air on the other end to be sickening, but it was far worse in the little pocket, a mere 2 metre high and 5 metres long. He pulled on the rope tied around his slippery torso, drawing it hand over hand until it was tight. \
\'93Sarah! Sarah?\'94 He called out but he heard no reply. \'93If you can hear me I made it. I will pull you through.\'94 The rope fell slack and he placed the shit-dribbling plasti-cable over his shoulder and walked towards dead-end of the tunnel. Sarah appeared out of the ooze looking as beautiful as ever. The sludge fell away onto the ground, her skin and hair purging itself of pathogens and dirt. \
 \
\'93Well, that was not pleasant.\'94 Sarah smiled, teeth gleaming white against her darkened, stained skin.\
\'93An interesting taste sensation to be sure.\'94 Cracker\'92s eyes made a decent attempt at popping out of his head as he gagged and dry wretched for several minutes before squatting on his haunches, spitting up watery saliva and drooling on his chin. \
\'93Let\'92s get to work, we have a nation to save.\'94 Sarah gently caressed her stomach, a wave of warmth and contentment pulsed through her hands and throughout her body. 
\f5\i Well, at least he seems to be happy I am here.
\f3\i0  \
\'93They have really outdone themselves. I never thought we would get this far. I am so proud of my Elvi.\'94 Cracker beamed.\
\'93Let\'92s not get too excited, we have to get through a metre on concrete and then contrive a way of destroying the labs and everything stored therein, without explosives.\'94\
The roof of the tunnel was the lumpy concrete underside of the laboratory basement floor, angry chunks of sharp aggregate jutting out into the airspace awaiting a tender scalp. At least they hoped they were under the laboratory in question. No doubt the maps and blueprints they had gathered together for this dig contained minor inaccuracies that could lead to major errors in the field. Having no other option than to trust the Elvi had excavated accurately, they scraped away the remaining clay and began drilling into the hard slab above. This concrete had been poured decades prior and had continued to harden as the years ticked by and even with giant impact drills and tungsten tipped bits the going was tediously slow.\
Breathing was difficult, nigh on impossible, but somehow their bodies managed to scrape together sufficient oxygen from the creeping yellow fog to support bodily functions. Their skin began firstly to tickle, then itch and burn as the smallest of scratches allowed gaseous acid to sear into their flesh, setting it ablaze. Pregnant or not, Sarah was determined to pull her own weight, easily keeping up with her muscular male counterpart, but unlike him, she never complained. \
To minimise effort and save time it was decided that they would make the smallest access hole possible sufficient to allow Cracker entry, but insufficient to accommodate Sarah and her tumescent belly. Eight hours solid work was rewarded with full penetration into the bowels of the laboratory complex. Cracker took a torch and climbed up through the concrete slab and disappeared. \
Sarah sat quietly with the remaining torch insipidly glowing in the rank vapours that swirled about as she wheezed each lungful of needles out. The access hole lit up and Cracker\'92s head poked down out of the roof as she heard muffled plasma bursts and screams from behind him.\
\'93They beat us here. The agents have taken over the facility. There are a few people in here we need to evacuate.\'94\
\'93How did they beat us? Why didn\'92t Agent Jones warn us?\'94\
\'93Ask him yourself. He\'92s coming with us.\'94 Cracker jumped down, followed by an armed Agent Jones. \'93Hurry Up! We have to get out of here.\'94 Sarah dived into the stench and disappeared, sliming her way to the other side where Elvi were waiting with buckets of warm water and fresh clothing. \
Professor Hermann dropped down from the tunnel roof with athletic ease as did the rest of his nimble team of subterranean survivalists Dr Anstey, Dr Millicent and Dr Ye. \
\'93There is no time to explain. Everyone has to jump into that raw sewage, dive 2 metres down and swim 15 metres straight ahead then two metres to the surface. It\'92s a giant U-bend and not unlike me, its full of shit. Can you guys hold your breath that long?\'94\
\'93Easily.\'94 Professor Hermann smugly scoffed. \'93We just want to get out of here.\'94 Without delay he and his colleagues entered the mire and happily dived down into the unknown.\
\'93They won\'92t be too far behind us. I\'92ve got one grenade and that\'92s all.\'94 Agent Jones coughed deeply from the bottom of his lungs, spitting up white chunks of tissue as his legs buckled under his weight. He gasped and wheezed for breath, but could not maintain consciousness. Shuffling feet above alerted Cracker to the imminent arrival of heavily armed company agents, ordered to clear the facility with extreme prejudice. He rolled Agent Jones on his back and unclipped the small grenade hanging from his belt and tied a loop of rope around his waist. The unconscious agent was dragged, supine into the swamp of effluent, while Cracker waited until the first agents dropped out of the ceiling. He tossed the grenade and dived under, dragging Agent Jones by the rope. The size of the explosion, combined with the the tiny space the expanding gas found itself in, insisted that the pressure be released by the path of least resistance. The floor of the basement above blew upward, slamming into the underside of the floor above, killing every agent in the room, but it did not stop there. Unrelieved, the compression wave pressed upon the pool of sewage with such force that the entire reservoir of liquid shit blew around the U-bend. Out the far end of the tunnel, Cracker, Agent Jones and a few hapless Elvi along with twenty thousand litres of liquid diarrhea shot out, horizontal to the ground where human sized nuggets slopped about in the black slush.\
\'93In the name of the Dawkins, hose them down.\'94 The team leader ordered. \'93Hurry up!\'94\
\'93Cracker? Which one is Cracker?\'94 Through the black paint, Sarah could not tell who was who.\
\'93I am the Great Teacher, Blessed Mother.\'94 Cracker stood up, fumes visibly rising off his frame in the dimly lit building site.\
\'93What happened in there?\'94\
\'93I found survivors. They\'92ve been there nearly 20 years! I let them tell you how they survived, but they told me the team of agents broke into the labs a few days ago. They are systematically clearing out the lab of everything, samples, files and equipment. I found the survivors hiding out, but luckily Agent Jones found us, he helped us all get back to the tunnel, he killed a couple of his own in the process.\'94\
\'93It\'92s over then. They\'92ve won. They have all they need to kill the off the Elvi.\'94 Resignation was not something Sarah ordinarily resorted to, but she felt she had no option other than to acknowledge a dead-end.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi720\sl360\slmult1\qc\partightenfactor0

