\f3\fs26 \'93Hello? I am told you two are in charge here.\'94 Professor Hermann apologetically interrupted as he continued to wiped the dark stains off his face. \'93Thank you for releasing us. We\'92ve been locked away five decades. These are my colleagues Dr Anstey, Dr Millicent and Dr Ye. And I am Professor\'85 \'94 \
\'93Hermann? Is that you? It can\'92t be. He would be at least..\'94\
\'9360 years old?\'94\
\'93Yes.\'94\
\'93I am Professor Andale Hermann, but how do you know me?\'94\
\'93I am Sarah Jacobson, Alana\'92s daughter. Do you remember me?\'94\
\'93Of course. But you would be nearly, 30 years old by now, wouldn\'92t you? And aren\'92t you just glowing\'94\
\'93Not too bad for 32, don\'92t you think?\'94\
\'93And your mother?\'94\
\'93She died in the great viral cleansing, 20 years ago, along with my sister.\'94\
\'93She died? I don\'92t understand.\'94 He was deeply shocked by this news. He had truly expected her to see her again. \'93You opened the package?\'94\uc0\u8232 \
\'93And drank the hemlock, Professor. I read part of the note, but I threw the rest out.\'94\
\'93Why would you do something like that?\'94 \
\'93I was 12 and from what I read, I took to the understanding that I had swallowed a vial full of semen. It was just inoculated water was it not?\'94 
\f5\i Please just be water.
\f3\i0 \
\'93Yes, inoculated saline solution. If you had read the whole thing you all would have been fine. Oh Alana.\'94 The news of Alana\'92s demise cut him deeply, perhaps permanently. \'93You killed her, you know that don\'92t you?\'94 \
\'93It is something I had not realised until very recently, Professor. Self-loathing is difficult to deflect and even more difficult to endure.\'94 \
\'93You could not have known.\'94\
\'93I swore if I ever saw you again I would beat you senseless. I spent years training in multiple martial arts disciplines, just in case I happened across you one day. I could not conceive of any story you could concoct that would ever excuse you for breaking my mother\'92s heart so cruelly.\'94\
\'93Have you infected many people? By the looks of you there must be at lease one\'94 He noted her taught little belly.\
\'93No, believe it or not, I have remained a virgin. However, I have infected one other. Cracker here, known to some as The Great Teacher, has also been infected. I think there may be one other, but I am not sure. I think she got it off Cracker.\'94\
\'93I haven\'92t touched anyone\'94 Cracker protested.\
\'93Kathy hugged you and kissed you in the morgue.\'94\
\'93Ah, yes. Kissing in the morgue. Good times.\'94 Cracker tried on sarcasm and it seemed to fit.\
\'93She examined your injuries too and dipped her hand in your blood.\'94\
\'93She has been looking mighty good lately, yeah.\'94 Cracker finally came around. \'93I can\'92t be blamed for that, I had just come back from the dead.\'94\
\'93The Hybrid T-virus brought you back from the dead?\'94 Professor Hermann was surprised. \'93I never thought the virus worked that well. That is amazing.\'94\
\'93I don\'92t think he was actually dead, just moribund.\'94 At no stage had Sarah actually thought Cracker had died. He was dragged back from the brink, not resurrected. \'93The point is I have remained a virgin for 32 years because I had no idea what I had contracted. From my personal experience it is entirely positive, but is that the case for everyone?\'94\
\'93The T-virus supercharges every system in the body. It slows and then reverses aging. It is a panacea for all human pathogens, no microbe can make you ill and there would be no need for any more expensive medicines. Jamison Hardy locked us in there because we would have destroyed the pharmaceuticals industry, so we have been working on other less damaging versions of the virus. We have had plenty of time to tinker and even made a virus to inoculate against the T-virus.\'94\
\'93I don\'92t want that\'94 Cracker protested. He was perfectly happy the way he was. \'93Keep it well away from me.\'94\
\'93It is not a cure, once you are infected you are infected for life.\'94\
\'93How are you not all insane? 20 years locked in a bunker? I wouldn\'92t last a week before I went nuts.\'94 Cracker, along with everyone else, found it difficult to understand how four people could live in in such proximity for so long with succumbing to neuroses of one sort or another.\
\'93It\'92s the T-virus, it has to be. I believe that its effect upon our physiology is so profound and our brain tissue is so sturdy, so perfect, that it shores up our psyche as well. Marvelous!\'94 Dr Hermann could offer up no other explanation. According to his knowledge of psychology they should have killed each other years ago.\
\'93What about food and water?\'94 Sarah was still unconvinced. \'9320 years without food or water?\'94\
\'93Each lab had its own separate air and water filtration and recirculation systems, we were never going to suffocate or die of thirst. Our biggest issue was food, but we had anticipated Mr Hardy\'92s reaction and had in place sufficient raw materials to grow proteins and vegetable matter in the lab. It is not something I would recommend eating. In fact, I would kill for a steak just about now.\'94\
\'93Elvis?\'94 Sarah called out. Ten or more tripped and pushed each other over as they ran to be the first to stand before the Blessed Mother. The losers of the race formed a small rabble behind the winner, still pushing and shoving. \'93Take Professor Hermann and his team to the High Elvis. They are to be treated as honoured guests. Get them cleaned up and fed, probably no steaks Professor, but it should be better than lab grown protein. The Great Teacher and I will meet you in Parliament House.\'94\
\'93What\'92s going on?\'94 Dr Anstey protested but didn\'92t fight, knowing she could destroy any ten of these identical drones at a whim. \'93Are you clones?\'94\
\'93Yes, ma\'92am. Elvis Clones.\'94\
\'93How very interesting.\'94 She said as she took him by the arm and slowly walked away. \'93What exactly is an Elvis?\'94\
\'93Much has changed in 20 years, professor. We were here, tonight, for a reason and we have failed in that important mission. We have to re-group and I think you may be able to provide some insight. You will be treated well and have access to the link. You can track down any relatives, but you cannot let it be known that you are alive. You will put yourselves and your family in grave danger.\'94 Sarah did not want these people wandering off and alerting the company to their existence. \'93Company agents are raping your facility for the purpose of developing a viral agent to kill 100,000 people, the entire Elvi nation.\'94 \
\'93I don\'92t know what an Elvi is, but killing a whole nation of them sounds a little excessive.\'94 Professor Hermann was happy to help and walked off slowly with a group of Elvis helpers, looking up and stretching his arms to the sky, still not quite believing he was free.\
\'93Morality is not a big thing, these days.\'94 Sarah sighed.\
\'9332 years old, eh?\'94 Cracker called out the elephant in the room. \'93Do you need a hand, grandma?\'94\uc0\u8232 \
\'93Very funny. See if you look so good in 10 years.\'94 \
\'93I probably won\'92t be pregnant.\'94 \
\'93No you won\'92t. What about him?\'94 Sarah pointed to Agent Jones who was coughing and vomiting up black ooze through his nose and mouth. \'93Of those who came out of the lab complex, he is the only one not protected by the T-virus. What should we do with him. He could be infected with anything. Why didn\'92t they give him a bio-suit?\'94\
\'93He had to take it off to fit through the hole we dug out. We will get two Elvi to take him back to their medical centre. All three will have to go into isolation until we know if they have anything nasty. Volunteers only for this one.\'94 \
\'93We need to get hold of Hayley and Kathy and meet at the Elvi Parliament. Whatever we do, we have to act fast.\'94\
\'93I\'92ll get these jokers to clean up as best they can and fix that pipe. There will be shit pouring out of the tunnel soon, unless I can get the boys here to dodgy-up a repair. Even if we are lucky, a repair like that won\'92t last long. I\'92ll meet you at parliament house as soon as I can.\'94 Cracker pointed at the open end of the tunnel, still seeping filth.\
\'93Make sure you have a few showers before you get there.\'94 Sarah said holding her nose. \'93Take as many as you have to.\'94\
\'93You don\'92t smell too good either.\'94 Cracker returned fire.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi720\sl360\slmult1\qc\partightenfactor0

